  "worked_solution": "The number of visitors $V(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $300%.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a=25$ is the total number of visitors initially\n\n- $r=3.0$ is the growth rate ($300%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in days) after launch\n\nThe formula for exponential growth is\n\n$$\nV=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $V(t)$ is\n\n$$\nV=25\\cdot (1+3.0)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we get\n\n$$\nV(t)=25\\cdot (4)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the total number of visitors after $3$ days, we evaluate the above for $t=3:$\n\n$$\nV(3)=25\\cdot (4)^{3}=25\\cdot 64=1600\n$$\n\nTherefore, the estimated number of visitors after $3$ days is $1600.$",
